{
  "dom_id": "step-e5885",
  "name": "Example: Multiplying a Column-Vector By a Row-Vector",
  "problem": "Compute the product \n $\\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n       -1 \\\n \t0 \\\n        -2\n \t\n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack\n\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n        2 & -5\n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack.$",
  "worked_solution": "Here, the first factor is a $3 \\times 1$ matrix and the second factor is a $1 \\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in the first matrix and $1$ row in the second matrix, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{3} \\times {\\color{green}\\fbox{1}} {\\color{green}\\checkmark} {\\color{green}\\fbox{1}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} = \n\t\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{3} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have\n\n$$\n\\eqalign {\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n       -1 \\\n \t0 \\\n        -2\n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack\n\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n        2 & -5\n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack\n\n\t&= \n\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n        (-1)\\cdot 2 & (-1)\\cdot (-5) \\\n        0\\cdot 2 & 0\\cdot (-5)\\\n        (-2)\\cdot 2 & (-2)\\cdot (-5)\n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack \\[5pt]\n\n\t&=\n\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n       -2 & 5 \\\n       0 &  0 \\\n       -4 &  10 \n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack \n}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
